iconsmith:test: 
iconsmith:test:   This is not a style guide you can drift away from. Off-spec geometry is unrepresentable in this language: there is no op that takes path data.
iconsmith:test: 
iconsmith:test:   ## The loop
iconsmith:test: 
iconsmith:test: + From the repository root, run `npm ci` and `npm run build:local` first.
iconsmith:test: + The commands below use the local build; no global executable is installed.
iconsmith:test: +
iconsmith:test:   1. Read the concept. Decide what object to draw — the object noun, not the intent. `search` is a magnifying glass.
iconsmith:test:   2. Pick a keyline (below) and write a `.icon` program.
iconsmith:test:   3. `iconsmith draw icon.icon > icon.svg` — parse errors go to stderr and the exit code is non-zero. Fix them before going on.
iconsmith:test:   4. `iconsmith lint icon.svg --keyline <name>` — fix every `error`. Warnings are a prompt to check a choice was made, not a rule.
iconsmith:test:   5. Look at the SVG rendered at 16px. Lint checks the spec, not the drawing: a centred rectangle of the right size lints perfectly and is an icon of nothing. Record your inspection; independent AI review determines acceptance under the frozen rubric.
iconsmith:test:   6. Finalize the exact inspected artifacts for independent review. Compiler correction and named visual repair have separate bounded allowances under the original deadline. Missing paperwork requests finalization only; uncertain evidence requests clarification only. A clean render alone is not acceptance.
iconsmith:test: 
iconsmith:test:   ```bash
iconsmith:test: - npx iconsmith draw cloud-check.icon > cloud-check.svg
iconsmith:test: - npx iconsmith lint cloud-check.svg --keyline wide
iconsmith:test: - npx iconsmith --output json lint cloud-check.svg   # machine-readable
iconsmith:test: - npx iconsmith new database -o database.svg
iconsmith:test: + npm run --silent iconsmith -- draw cloud-check.icon > cloud-check.svg
iconsmith:test: + npm run --silent iconsmith -- lint cloud-check.svg --keyline wide
iconsmith:test: + npm run --silent iconsmith -- --output json lint cloud-check.svg   # machine-readable
iconsmith:test: + npm run --silent iconsmith -- new database -o database.svg
iconsmith:test:   ```
iconsmith:test: 
iconsmith:test:   `iconsmith new` is the product path: cheap host experts (compile / mark / analog) first, the gateway or OpenRouter agent only if they fail. Third-party packs (Lucide, Heroicons, Tabler, Remix) contribute _names_ for inventory, never drawings. `iconsmith improve --control analog --treatment agent --class pack-inventory --concepts …` is the A/B that updates that routing table. Do not paste Lucide path data into a program.
iconsmith:test: 
iconsmith:test:   `draw` writes SVG on stdout and diagnostics on stderr, so the redirect above always produces a valid file. Both commands exit non-zero on an error and 0 on warnings alone. Every command takes `--output json`; the default text output is for humans.
